\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Distribution of fragmentation scales from 3,240 linear perturbation theory parameter space calculations. The green shaded region indicates the observed projected 2D range ($2$--$3\times W_{\rm  fil}$) from HGBS measurements. The red dashed line shows the classical IM92 prediction ($4\times W_{\rm  fil}$). Approximately 20.6\% of calculations (667 out of 3,240) fall in this range without observational constraints. Note: The observed range is shown as projected 2D values as measured; 3D deprojected values would be approximately 1.27× larger due to geometric projection effects.}}{24}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:distribution}{{1}{24}{Distribution of fragmentation scales from 3,240 linear perturbation theory parameter space calculations. The green shaded region indicates the observed projected 2D range ($2$--$3\times W_{\rm fil}$) from HGBS measurements. The red dashed line shows the classical IM92 prediction ($4\times W_{\rm fil}$). Approximately 20.6\% of calculations (667 out of 3,240) fall in this range without observational constraints. Note: The observed range is shown as projected 2D values as measured; 3D deprojected values would be approximately 1.27× larger due to geometric projection effects}{figure.1}{}}
