\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Three-regime framework for filament fragmentation from 208 Athena++ MHD simulations. The colored contours show density contrast $C \equiv \rho _{\rm  max}/\rho _0$ as a function of Mach number $\mathcal  {M}$ and plasma $\beta $. Three distinct regimes are identified: (I) Magnetically subcritical ($\beta \lesssim 0.15$, green): minimal fragmentation with $C \approx 1$; (II) Magnetically regulated ($0.2 \lesssim \beta \lesssim 2$, blue): intermediate fragmentation with $C = 3.4$--$11$; (III) Thermally dominated ($\beta \gtrsim 3$, red): vigorous fragmentation with $C = 13$--$22$. The white rectangle indicates the parameter range for the W3 filament complex ($\mathcal  {M} = 2.5$--$3.5$, $\beta = 0.5$--$1.5$), where simulations reproduce the observed density contrast range of $C = 5$--$10$. The hatched region shows where the observed HGBS spacing of $\lambda /W \approx 2$ is reproduced.}}{47}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:regime_diagram_mhd}{{5}{47}{Three-regime framework for filament fragmentation from 208 Athena++ MHD simulations. The colored contours show density contrast $C \equiv \rho _{\rm max}/\rho _0$ as a function of Mach number $\mathcal {M}$ and plasma $\beta $. Three distinct regimes are identified: (I) Magnetically subcritical ($\beta \lesssim 0.15$, green): minimal fragmentation with $C \approx 1$; (II) Magnetically regulated ($0.2 \lesssim \beta \lesssim 2$, blue): intermediate fragmentation with $C = 3.4$--$11$; (III) Thermally dominated ($\beta \gtrsim 3$, red): vigorous fragmentation with $C = 13$--$22$. The white rectangle indicates the parameter range for the W3 filament complex ($\mathcal {M} = 2.5$--$3.5$, $\beta = 0.5$--$1.5$), where simulations reproduce the observed density contrast range of $C = 5$--$10$. The hatched region shows where the observed HGBS spacing of $\lambda /W \approx 2$ is reproduced}{figure.5}{}}
